# Line endings.
#
# Git on Windows converts LF to CRLF on checkout by default. That is harmless
# for most files here, but `scripts/backup.sh` is mounted straight into a Linux
# container and run by `sh`: with CRLF the shell reads `\r` as part of every
# command and the backup service dies on the first line. The same applies to
# anything else Linux executes verbatim.
#
# `text=auto` normalises to LF inside the repository; the `eol=lf` entries below
# additionally force LF in the working copy, so a checkout on Windows still
# produces files Linux can run.

* text=auto

*.sh        text eol=lf
*.mjs       text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
Caddyfile   text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.sql       text eol=lf
.env*       text eol=lf

# Binary — never touched.
*.png       binary
*.woff2     binary
*.ico       binary
